          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വിവാഹം — vivāhaṁ — \"a marriage; a wedding\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അവരുടെ വിവാഹം അടുത്ത മാസമാണ്. avaruṭe vivāhaṁ aṭutta māsamāṇŭ. Their wedding is next month."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The formal word beside കല്യാണം; invitations and the news use വിവാഹം (vivāhaṁ)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വിവാഹം (vivāhaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit vivāha, \"marriage\" (CDIAL 11920), from vi-vah, \"to lead away\": the bride was led from her father's house."
            }
          ]
        },
